<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Momine Khatun Mausoleum</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1186</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Momine Khatun Mausoleum is a ten-sided brick tomb tower in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nakhchivan">Nakhchivan</a>, completed in 1186 by the architect Ajami Nakhchivani for Momine Khatun, wife of the atabeg Eldiguz, on the orders of her son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jahan-pahlavan">Jahan Pahlavan</a>. Covered in carved geometric ornament, turquoise glaze and Kufic inscriptions, it still stands about 25 metres high and is the best-known monument of the Nakhchivan school of medieval architecture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/momine-khatun-mausoleum.jpg" alt="Momine Khatun Mausoleum" width="320" height="459" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sefer azeri · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M%C3%B6m%C3%BCn%C9%99xatun_t%C3%BCrb%C9%99si_2018.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
